@startuml

start

:TCMS executes on preemptive RTOS;
:Manage via deterministic, priority-scheduled tasks;
fork
  :Traction;
fork again
  :Braking;
fork again
  :Door control;
fork again
  :System diagnostics;
end fork

if (Detect train overspeed condition?) then (yes)
  :Verify emergency braking arming criteria;
  :Continuously poll status of trackside signal lights via high-priority monitoring task;
  if (Signal anomaly?) then (yes)
    :Trigger immediate emergency response;
    :Initiate concurrent operations;
    fork
      :ISR-driven process acquires track sensor data for real-time;
      :Upload to central control unit via CAN bus with CRC protection;
    fork again
      :Parallel safety task;
      :With mutex-protected access to shared sensor ring buffer;
      :Assess headway to forward obstacle against safe envelope;
    end fork
  else (no)
  end if

  :Proceed to next phase of safety assessment cycle;
  :Spawn parallel tasks;
  fork
    :Continuously monitor traction force;
  fork again
    :Continuously monitor braking performance;
  end fork
  :Whether within certified operational bounds;

  :Timer-interrupt-driven telemetry task archives system state to non-volatile memory;
  :Employ exponential backoff for transient communication faults;

else (no)
end if

:Independent watchdog timers and PMIC monitoring enforce system integrity;
:Ensure fail-safe degradation in compliance with EN 50128/EN 50129;

stop

@enduml
